{
  "$schema": "dsbench/v1",
  "name": "Coyote-Trial05",
  "citation": "Goldwire, H.C. et al. (1983). Coyote series data report - LLNL/NWC 1981 LNG spill tests dispersion, vapor burn, and rapid-phase-transition. LLNL UCID-19953. Trial 5. Parameters from PHMSA MVD Rev B 2024 Table 2-14.",
  "dataConfidence": "High",
  "description": "Coyote Trial 5 - LNG spill on water, dispersion phase before ignition. 22.8 m^3 LNG over 98 s (~96 kg/s). Frenchman Flat 1981. Wind 7.4 m/s, stability D. Companion to Coyote 3 with different stability and slightly larger pool. Sensors on arcs at 140, 300, 400 m, ~1 m height. Sensor values approximate from Hansen 2010 validation figures (confidence medium-low). DATA UPDATE: sensor values replaced by the PHMSA LNG Model Validation Database maximum arc-wise concentrations (short averaging time, 1 s) as tabulated in DNV, 'LNG Validation for UDM 6.6', report to PHMSA (Oct 2010), Table 9: 140 m: 11.53 mol%, 200 m: 8.09 mol%, 300 m: 3.17 mol%, 400 m: 2.30 mol%. Long-averaging (90 s) values for reference: 140 m: 3.03 mol%, 200 m: 2.47 mol%, 300 m: 0.85 mol%, 400 m: 0.57 mol%. Mass fractions converted with CH4/air molar masses.",
